cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this playbook or the copier script, please cite it as below."
title: "VMFS Recovery: recovering VMware VMs from a bare VMFS6 datastore disk via WSL2"
abstract: >-
  A field-tested playbook and interactive Bash script for recovering VMware
  virtual machines from a VMFS6 datastore disk that has been removed from an
  ESXi host and attached to a Windows PC over USB. Windows cannot read VMFS, so
  the disk is passed into WSL2 with usbipd-win and mounted with vmfs6-fuse.
  vmfs-copy.sh then copies each VM folder out, routing large -flat.vmdk disk
  images through GNU ddrescue (bad-sector retries, resumable via mapfile) and
  small .vmx, .nvram, and descriptor files through rsync, with folder detection,
  interactive selection, a live progress bar, a free-space check, and per-folder
  verification. Covers crash and power-loss recovery mid-copy, and registering
  the recovered VM on an ESXi 8 host.
